# guIDE GROUNDRULES are mandatory (not optional memory)

**Source of truth:** [`GROUNDRULES.md`](../../GROUNDRULES.md) at the guIDE repo root.  
**Mirror / tripwire extract:** [`notes/guide3/RULES.md`](../../notes/guide3/RULES.md).

Read with the Read tool every guIDE turn — never rely on conversation memory.

## When to read

| Trigger | Action |
|---------|--------|
| Session start / user assigns guIDE work | Read `GROUNDRULES.md` full |
| Before **any** code edit | Re-read §0–§3 + §5 |
| Before **any** fix / architecture suggestion | Reject if it hides tokens, hardcodes one task, unloads Cipher, or is a cheap workaround |
| After operator issues a forever constraint | **Update `GROUNDRULES.md` the same turn** |

## Non-negotiable (violations = rejected work)

- Universal Cursor-clone IDE — no task/file/domain hardcodes
- **Never hide / strip / hold** model output — route channels only
- Cipher stays **GPU-resident on P40** unless operator explicitly orders unload
- No cheap workarounds; no stacked symptom patches
- Status chrome must not split sentences or lie about “first token”

## Suggestions and plans

Before presenting a plan, verify it does not violate `GROUNDRULES.md` §0–§3. If it resembles strip/hold/hide or a one-file hardcode, do not suggest it.
